gaht(){return"Public profile"},
gahs(){return"The \u201cShare my profile\u201d setting, off at first, publishes a read-only page on the Mirinu relay: the name you pick and, for each title of the chosen types, its name, year, poster, status, whether it is in your favorites and your rating out of 10, with totals and the day of the last update. The app updates it at most once an hour, when your library changes. It is the only data Mirinu keeps in the clear: anyone with the link can read it. Your personal notes, watch dates and devices are never in it. The link is drawn at random, the page is closed to search engines, and its posters come from TMDB's servers."},
gahu(){return"This sharing rests on your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR). Stopping it withdraws that consent: the app erases the page from the relay as soon as it reaches it, and keeps trying while offline; someone who opened it may keep it for up to a minute in their browser. A page the app has not updated for 180 days is erased. The relay then keeps a fingerprint of the link, and nothing else, for 2 years so it cannot be used again."},
